/-- **The numerator half of "duplication composes with multiplication by `n`"**:

```
Φ₂ₙ = Φₙ⁴ − b₄Φₙ²ΨSqₙ² − 2b₆ΦₙΨSqₙ³ − b₈ΨSqₙ⁴      in R[X].
```

The right-hand side is `Φ₂ = X⁴ − b₄X² − 2b₆X − b₈` homogenised at `(Φₙ, ΨSqₙ)`, so together with
`WeierstrassCurve.HasΨSqDoubling` — which does the same for the denominator `Ψ₂Sq` — this says that
the duplication map applied to the `n`-division coordinates gives the `2n`-division coordinates,
numerator and denominator separately.

⚠️ **This is not a weaker statement than the crux and it is not a step towards it.**  Every
measurement in the module docstring puts it on exactly the same footing as
`WeierstrassCurve.HasΨSqDoubling`: same failure as a free identity in the `bᵢ` from `n = 2` onwards,
same exact divisibility by `4b₈ − b₂b₆ + b₄²`, cofactors of the same size to within one term. -/
def HasΦDoubling (n : ℤ) : Prop :=
  W.Φ (2 * n) = W.Φ n ^ 4 - C W.b₄ * W.Φ n ^ 2 * W.ΨSq n ^ 2 -
    2 * C W.b₆ * W.Φ n * W.ΨSq n ^ 3 - C W.b₈ * W.ΨSq n ^ 4


